237: | da-g5-respond | Meaning from movement patterns; what makes a dance artistic | da-g6-respond (unit 3) | A written critique with criteria the student drafts |
238: | da-g5-stage | One dance adapted to two spaces | da-g6-stage (unit 4) | Moves adapted to the space, performance manners, the choreographer's notes, production elements explained |
239: | da-g5-connect | A dance from another subject's topic; a style's quality and its culture | da-g6-connect (unit 4) | A viewpoint on a researched social issue danced; a dance's cultural meaning interpreted |
248: | Elements | da-g6-elements (unit 1, days 1 to 18) | da-g7-elements (unit 5): body designs borrowed from other styles, accents and variations, qualities compared | da-g8-elements (unit 9) retrieves da-g7-elements (unit 5, days 65 to 82): shapes around dancers, props and the room, separate tempos, textured energy | Spacing and measures, then borrowing and accents, then sculpting and layering |
249: | Technique and rehearsal | da-g6-technique (unit 1, days 1 to 18) | da-g7-technique (unit 5): technique adapted to growing bodies, healthy habits discussed, group goals after watching professionals | da-g8-technique (unit 9) retrieves da-g7-technique (unit 5, days 65 to 82): recalled spatial and rhythmic phrases, habits evaluated, personal goals and a progress record | Clean transitions and a warm-up, then adapting and group goals, then accuracy and a personal record |
250: | Ideas | da-g6-ideas (unit 2, days 19 to 32) | da-g7-ideas (unit 6): sources compared, styles chosen for an aim and explained | da-g8-ideas (unit 10) retrieves da-g7-ideas (unit 6, days 83 to 96): the student's own strongest moves for an original dance, justified | Joined, then compared and chosen, then owned and defended |
251: | Shape of a study | da-g6-form (unit 2, days 19 to 32) | da-g7-form (unit 6): a study shaped with several tools and forms, criteria explained | da-g8-form (unit 10) retrieves da-g7-form (unit 6, days 83 to 96): a group dance, the group process described, criteria applied | A goal stated, then choices explained, then made with others |
252: | Revising and notation | da-g6-revise (unit 3, days 35 to 48) | da-g7-revise (unit 7): revisions weighed against shifting standards, an established notation tried | da-g8-revise (unit 11) retrieves da-g7-revise (unit 7, days 99 to 112): revision alone or shared, an excerpt notated | Group criteria and an invented notation, then weighed revisions and an established method, then an excerpt |
253: | Responding | da-g6-respond (unit 3, days 35 to 48) | da-g7-respond (unit 7): patterns and elements compared across styles, meanings compared, criteria refined | da-g8-respond (unit 11) retrieves da-g7-respond (unit 7, days 99 to 112): evidence for a judgment of an effective performance | Criteria built, then compared and refined, then used for a judgment with evidence |
254: | Performing and production | da-g6-stage (unit 4, days 49 to 62) | da-g7-stage (unit 8): space adaptations recommended, a rehearsal journal, another venue explored | da-g8-stage (unit 12) retrieves da-g7-stage (unit 8, days 113 to 126): students lead preparation and design staging for two spaces | Manners and notes, then a journal and a venue, then leading and designing |
255: | Connecting | da-g6-connect (unit 4, days 49 to 62) | da-g7-connect (unit 8): a style's history and spirit, dances from different places compared | da-g8-connect (unit 12) retrieves da-g7-connect (unit 8, days 113 to 126): two topics researched and choreographed, dances of many cultures and eras analyzed | One issue and one dance's meaning, then a style's history and two places, then two topics and many eras |
