323: | 10 | 8 | Making it together. *How does a group turn many sources into an original dance, and how do we know our criteria worked?* | 14 | da-g8-ideas; da-g8-form | DA:Cr1.1.8a; DA:Cr1.1.8b; DA:Cr2.1.8a; DA:Cr2.1.8b | Creating (Cr1, Cr2); responding practiced on the works (review). Works: a dance by Pilobolus the unit plan picks (United States, a company founded in 1971 by students who made every dance together), group-made shapes, described and linked to the company's page; Germaine Acogny, Somewhere at the Beginning (Senegal, 2015; Acogny born 1944, founder of the École des Sables, the unit plan records whether living, as of its date), a dance from her own life and her grandmother's, described and linked | Retrieval in day 2's warm-up: grade 7 sources compared and styles chosen (da-g7-ideas, unit 6) and a study shaped with explained criteria (da-g7-form, unit 6). DA:Cr1.1.8a: turn varied inspirations into movement material for a dance study. DA:Cr1.1.8b: pick the student's own strongest moves for an original dance and justify the picks with style terms. DA:Cr2.1.8a: with a group, choose choreographic tools and a form for a new dance and describe how the group worked (who led, how choices were made, one disagreement settled). DA:Cr2.1.8b: define and apply criteria for a personal or cultural dance (an invented dancer's or a public figure's option marked the same) and discuss their effect on the piece. Words: material, original, justify, collaborate, process, effect. Showing: the group dances for another class. End-of-unit evidence (two check days), id by id: DA:Cr1.1.8a, the kept material page: three sources and the movement material each gave; DA:Cr1.1.8b, a written item on the written day: three moves picked for the original dance, each justified with a style term; DA:Cr2.1.8a, a guide look-for on the group showing (tools and form seen), with the kept process note; DA:Cr2.1.8b, the kept criteria sheet: criteria defined, applied to the group dance, and one effect discussed. Each item is marked met, partly or not yet. Out: an artist's statement (Level 1). Tools: the material page, the style menu, the process note, the criteria sheet, Curio Class's own. Free path: printed source cards. Once-a-week path: 8 sessions | After unit 9 because the group dance draws on its sculpted shapes and layered time; before unit 11, which revises this dance and notates an excerpt | Candidate: a group-made dance by a company from Asia, for range | Acogny's dance tells her own family story; the sensitivity agent reads her school's and a museum's pages first, and no student is asked to dance their own family story: an invented dancer's or a public figure's option is marked the same. Group process: the process note names roles and choices, never blame. Pilobolus shapes include supported balances: the class keeps to shapes with no lifts, no one's weight carried, contact only by agreement, with a solo version of every shape. Health's steps if a student tells something. Agent reads: sensitivity; safety (hands-on). |
